# A diner
Someone at the table:  their name, what they ordered, and what they owe.
Each diner is its own element on the page, a row of Spell UI's fields bound to it:
typing a name or an amount changes the diner, and every sum follows.

<spell-view "diner">
	<property "name">text</>
	<property "amount" type="number" description="What they ordered, before the tip"/>
	<property "tip" description="Their share of the tip:  the same part of it as their part of the bill">the amount * bill splitter's percent / 100</>
	<property "share" description="What they owe">the amount + the tip</>

	<action "remove it" description="Takes them off the bill">remove it from bill splitter's diners</>

	<draw description="Their name, their amount, what they owe, and a button to take them off">
		<form value={it}>
			<stack direction="horizontal" spacing="sm">
				<input name="name" placeholder="Name" aria-label="Name"/>
				<input name="amount" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" aria-label="Amount" label="$"/>
				<space fluid/>
				<text bold>{write the share as money}</text>
				<button icon="close" appearance="basic" aria-label="Remove" onClick={remove it}/>
			</stack>
		</form>
	</draw>
</spell-view>

<spell-view "table" template="viewable list of diners" description="The diners, one a row">
	<draw "placeholder">
		<text color="grey">Nobody yet:  add someone</text>
	</draw>
</spell-view>

<spell>
	// a diner sits at one table
	a diner belongs to one table
</spell>
